  "story": "Keep the story: up to eight chronological frames and a prompt focused on the main activity and supported changes. 768px previews reduce model input; 256 output tokens bound the caption. Four-frame variants lost event detail; literal frame-by-frame prompts were less useful for recall. Replaying clips inflated RTX gains, so its final comparison resets the model cache and warms on synthetic frames. Live charts below track fresh production work.",
  "method": "Six fixed clips, 5.8–376.9 seconds. Short-clip frame cap and JPEG resizing match production. RTX: two requests, model-runtime reset and synthetic warmup before each cell; load/warmup excluded. Mac: warm server with prompt caching disabled; old four-request configuration vs selected concurrency. Caption cache bypassed. Media decode is precomputed for model trials. Shared homelab hardware; not a controlled quality benchmark.",
  "reviewed": 12,
  "quality": "Manual comparison against six eight-frame contact sheets. Accepted for main-activity/event recall with remaining minor inferred details; not a blind accuracy score. No speech transcription is installed. Reconciliation still handles text disagreements.",
